          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimplicialSets"} SimplicialSets
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
            between two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            is often called the
            %em function complex
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complex"} simplicial complex
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            = succeed "\u201D)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+complex"} function complex
            of two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            is the collection of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps"} maps
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopies"} left homotopies
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+homotopies"} higher homotopies
            between them, all itself organized into a simplicial set.
          %p
            More formally,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimplicialSets"} SimplicialSets
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+monoidal+category"} Cartesian monoidal category
            and the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            is what is traditionally known as the function complex.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#GeneralDefinition General
          %p
            Suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            that admits small
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
          %p
            Given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,A\in \mathcal{C}^{\Delta^{op}}
            %strong function complex
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
